      "diff": "@@ -24,17 +24,62 @@ It is used for troubleshooting, analysis, development and education.\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n-// The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n+The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-// * wssalink:2021-16[]\n-// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n+* wssalink:2021-16[]\n+Gryphon dissector crash.\n+wsbuglink:17737[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: ca71d1624c\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 2836470b73\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 86ea1cc4fd\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-476: NULL Pointer Dereference\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2021-11-18-10827.pcap wsbuglink:17737[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-17[]\n+RTMPT dissector infinite loop.\n+wsbuglink:17745[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: 80ebcc90bc\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 614184a7df\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 36c3ff8596\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-835: Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2021-11-23-8582.pcap wsbuglink:17745[].\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2021-11-25-10735.pcap wsbuglink:17749[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-18[]\n+BitTorrent DHT dissector infinite loop.\n+wsbuglink:17754[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: ebcba787a0\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 6f90eb902e\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: ddd4114305\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-835: Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')\n+// * Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2021-11-29-6844.pcap wsbuglink:17754[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-20[]\n+RFC 7468 dissector infinite loop.\n+wsbuglink:17801[].\n+// cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n+// Fixed in master: b3215d99ca\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: 918ca332e8\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: 33ff19e11f\n+// CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n+// CWE-835: Loop with Unreachable Exit Condition ('Infinite Loop')\n+// * Freeze on opening an incomplete RFC 7468 file wsbuglink:17801[].\n+\n+* wssalink:2021-21[]\n+Sysdig Event dissector crash.\n // wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n // cveidlink:2021-xxxxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: xxxxx\n-// Fixed in release-3.6: xxxxx\n-// Fixed in release-3.4: xxxxx\n+// Fixed in master: c22b8bcb5f\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: a09a47036b\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: d2436f19a3\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n-// CWE-xxx\n+// CWE-126: Buffer Over-read\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -44,6 +89,14 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* Wireshark exposed details your sordid redneck past, which were subsequently widely disseminated on social media.\n // cp /dev/null /tmp/buglist.txt ; for bugnumber in `git log v3.4.4rc0.. | gsed -e 's/\\(close\\|fix\\|resolv\\)[^ ]* #/\\nclose #/gI' | grep ^close | sed -e 's/close.*#\\([1-9][0-9]*\\).*/\\1/' | sort -V -u` ; do \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/tools/gen-bugnote\" $bugnumber; pbpaste >> /tmp/buglist.txt; done\n \n+* 43 test case failed in Ubuntu Build action wsbuglink:17730[].\n+\n+* 5GS TAI not correctly decoded for GTPv2 wsbuglink:17738[].\n+\n+* Can't install \"ChmodBPF.pkg\" or \"Add Wireshark to the system path.pkg\" on M1 MacBook Air Monterey without Rosetta 2 wsbuglink:17757[].\n+\n+* Unable to build without tshark wsbuglink:17766[].\n+\n === New and Updated Features\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n@@ -66,6 +119,19 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.4.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n+AT\n+BT-DHT\n+BT LE LL\n+EVS\n+FF\n+Gryphon\n+GTPv2\n+MKA\n+RFC 7468\n+RTMPT\n+RTSP\n+SRVLOC\n+Sysdig Event\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n",
